      "message": "I\u0027ll defer to the SWEs who have to maintain this code, but I thought the appropriate way to mix tabs and spaces is to use space to align and tab to indent.  So in this instance you have\n\n#define STM32_TIM_CR1(n)...........STM32_TIM_REG(n, 0x00)\n\nso you\u0027d want to do the following with a single tab:\n\n#define STM32_TIM_CR1_CEN..........-\u003e\tBIT(0)\n\nthis works regardless of tabstop size\n\n    #define STM32_TIM_CR1(n)...........STM32_TIM_REG(n, 0x00)\n(2) #define STM32_TIM_CR1_CEN..........-\u003eBIT(0)\n(4) #define STM32_TIM_CR1_CEN..........-\u003e  BIT(0)\n(8) #define STM32_TIM_CR1_CEN..........-\u003e      BIT(0)\n\nwhereas the way currently written would break\n\n    #define STM32_TIM_CR1(n)...........STM32_TIM_REG(n, 0x00)\n(t) #define STM32_TIM_CR1_CEN-\u003e\t-\u003e\tBIT(0)\n(2) #define STM32_TIM_CR1_CEN-\u003e-\u003eBIT(0)\n(4) #define STM32_TIM_CR1_CEN-\u003e  -\u003e  BIT(0)\n(8) #define STM32_TIM_CR1_CEN-\u003e      -\u003e      BIT(0)",
